<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chaldean Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Neo-Babylonian Empire, Neo-Babylonian, Chaldeans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chaldean Empire, also known as the Neo-Babylonian Empire, was a Mesopotamian state centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>, founded in 626 BCE by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nabopolassar">Nabopolassar</a>. Allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medes">Medes</a>, it destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nebuchadnezzar-ii">Nebuchadnezzar II</a> dominated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a> and rebuilt Babylon. It was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrus-the-great">Cyrus the Great</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> in 539 BCE.</p></div>
